From b4a00b6eecfed348147f37e2d50521c039ccde9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:28:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-113: the zoomWheel setting -- which wheel zooms,
 as WPF's "Zoom by using" (0.113.0)

WPF (Tools > Options > XAML Designer) lets you pick what zooms the artboard:
Ctrl+mouse wheel, the mouse wheel alone, or Alt+mouse wheel. Here it was always
Ctrl+wheel. New setting ht9045Designer.zoomWheel = ctrl (the default, as before)
/ wheel / alt; a change reaches the open designers at once. When Ctrl is not the
zoom key, Ctrl+wheel scrolls (never the webview's own page zoom). The status
bar's tip names the key in use.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 189, panels, real VS Code 159):
probe (alt: Ctrl+wheel only scrolls, Alt+wheel 1 -> 1.1; wheel: the wheel 1 ->
1.1, Shift+wheel does not zoom; back to ctrl: the wheel does not zoom); smoke
(init says ctrl; set to alt -> wheelZoom sent at once, the tip says Alt+wheel).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
